;; The six awai businesses and the role set each one needs.
;;
;; MEMBERSHIP, not activity — `fleet.edn` governs how many may run at once.
;;
;; ## Why :roles-absent exists
;;
;; `yakuwari.spec` refuses a role with no objective, because a role nobody
;; can state the purpose of is not reviewable. The same argument applies to
;; absence: a business missing a `sales` role and a business that never
;; considered one look identical unless the omission is stated. So every
;; business lists what it deliberately does NOT have and why, and a reviewer
;; can disagree with a sentence instead of guessing at a gap.
;;
;; Adding a business is one entry here plus one file under yakuwari/.

{:awai.businesses/version 1
 :awai.businesses/roles-vocabulary
 {:director "sets what this business is trying to do next, and is the party outward correspondence reaches"
  :engineer "changes the product; proposes patches, never merges them"
  :designer "owns the product's presentation and interaction"
  :sales "converts a named prospect into a paying customer"
  :marketer "makes the product findable and legible to people who have not heard of it"
  :supporter "answers the people already using it"}

 ;; sales and supporter and director correspond OUTWARD — they hold a
 ;; mailbox and a did:web (owner decision 2026-07-30). engineer, designer and
 ;; marketer are definitions only: marketer publishes, but it publishes
 ;; through the product's own channels rather than as a correspondent, so it
 ;; needs no mailbox of its own.
 :awai.businesses/outward-roles #{:director :sales :supporter}

 :awai.businesses/businesses
 [{:business/id :network-isekai
   :business/name "network isekai"
   :business/repo "network-awai/network-isekai"
   :business/domain "isekai.network"
   :business/what "Play and fork CLJ/EDN games in the browser — CodePen for games. A game is data: an EDN scene plus Clojure-subset logic, forkable as a kotoba-git commit."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :designer :marketer :supporter]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :sales
     :why "An open creator platform has no named prospects to convert — growth is people forking games, not a pipeline. Add sales if a paid tier for studios ships."}]}

  {:business/id :club-shinshi
   :business/name "club shinshi"
   :business/repo "network-awai/club-shinshi"
   :business/domain "shinshi.club"
   :business/what "Membership club. Operated by JK Inc. (BVI); shared contracts, legal and operations live in the root repo while the app and its two actor modules are siblings."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :designer :sales :marketer :supporter]
   :business/roles-absent []
   :business/note "The only business carrying all six. Membership is sold to named people, so sales is a real function rather than a funnel."}

  {:business/id :net-babiniku
   :business/name "net babiniku"
   :business/repo "network-awai/net-babiniku"
   :business/domain "babiniku.net"
   :business/what "Chat with an AI character whose body is a live-rendered VRM avatar — VTuber presentation rather than a static portrait. An LLM-persona node proposes {:dialogue :emotion :motion-cue}; a governor is the only path to a renderable turn."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :designer :marketer :supporter]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :sales
     :why "Consumer self-serve. Nobody is negotiated with, so there is nothing for a sales role to do that marketer and supporter do not already cover."}]}

  {:business/id :net-kotobase
   :business/name "net kotobase"
   :business/repo "network-awai/net-kotobase"
   :business/domain "kotobase.net"
   :business/what "Content-addressed knowledge-graph BaaS, pinning and hosting. Three plans separated by who carries operational responsibility: P2P, Secure Managed (99.9% SLA with credits), Enterprise (99.999%, by contract)."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :sales :marketer :supporter]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :designer
     :why "The product surface is an API, runbooks and plan documents — presentation work here is documentation, which engineer and marketer own between them. Add a designer when a console ships."}]
   :business/note "Enterprise is sold by contract, so sales is real. The SLA makes supporter's incident duty load-bearing rather than courteous."}

  {:business/id :app-aozora
   :business/name "app aozora"
   :business/repo "network-awai/app-aozora"
   :business/domain "aozora.app"
   :business/what "The canonical AT Protocol boundary for the fleet: PDS, AppView, XRPC adapter, feeds, search and actor profile publication. Domain repos publish through it rather than running their own PDS."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :designer :supporter :marketer]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :sales
     :why "Infrastructure the fleet's own organisms depend on, not a product sold to outsiders. Its consumers are sibling repos, which do not need converting."}]}

  {:business/id :nexus-x402
   :business/name "nexus x402"
   :business/repo "network-awai/nexus-x402"
   :business/domain "x402.nexus"
   :business/what "Self-hosted x402 payment facilitator and gateway — the sovereign equivalent of a closed monetization gateway, live with three registered sellers. The facilitator holds no keys; each seller settles to its own treasury."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :sales :marketer :supporter]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :designer
     :why "The directory page and llms.txt renderer come from kotoba-lang/x402-directory; this repo adds only a thin branding layer, so there is no presentation surface of its own to own."}]
   :business/note "Sellers are onboarded one at a time by name — sales here is seller onboarding, not end-user acquisition."}]}
